# {{name}}

An Ananke quickstart project scaffolded with `nnke new quickstart`.

## Run it

```bash
dotnet run
```

No API key required — this project uses `SimulatedModel`, which returns a hardcoded
response so you can see the workflow machinery working without credentials.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{name}}.csproj` | .NET project — references `Ananke.Orchestration` only |
| `Program.cs` | Workflow + agent job + SimulatedModel (swap for real provider when ready) |
| `QuickstartState.cs` | Typed state record threaded through the workflow |

No `.ananke.yml` — this project is pure C#. Manifest-driven topology comes next.

## Switch to a real LLM provider

See the commented-out provider blocks at the bottom of `Program.cs`. The steps:

1. Add the provider package, e.g.:
   ```bash
   dotnet add package Ananke.Orchestration.OpenAI
   ```
2. Add your API key to a `secrets.json`:
   ```json
   { "OpenAI": { "ApiKey": "sk-..." } }
   ```
3. Replace `SimulatedModel` with the provider model (see `Program.cs` comments).

Full walkthrough: `nnke docs 01-getting-started`

